  "problem": "Independent exact-head review of 9947794 found colliding publisher release IDs, reusable-over-time distribution collapse, vintage-as-global-release, unbound pin/publication mismatches, unrelated resources attachment, order-dependent date conflicts, invented dictionary revision identity, and a stale identity package seal (file_count 25 vs 30).",
  "resulting_behavior": "Correction commit d6c82c71fed88e91f0e7957103998f114db70b33 keeps original C-007-1/2/3 history. Publisher namespace/punctuation/long values stay distinct; reusable-over-time identifiers are not immutable IDs; c_vintage is not a global release ID; publication/map/record ownership bind together; unrelated resources require a captured link; conflicting date literals remain inspectable; dictionary revision stays unresolved rather than copying the generation label; the current identity package seal matches exact current bytes. Frozen contract pins and automatic_rule_state=disabled_candidate_only are unchanged. Execution.provider grok, dispatch model grok-4; this interface is Grok 4.6 and is not a serving-model attestation.",
